WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.130
- Welcome back everybody.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.340
I'm hanging out with magician
Asi Wind and Idina Menzel.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.515
Give it up.

00:00:06.515 --> 00:00:08.340
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.190
So, as most of you know, I'm
passionate about writing.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.510
It's the reason we teamed up

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.710
with our season-long partner

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.020
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,
the go-to erasable pen

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.490
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.480
and the preferred pen

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.836
for those fearlessly
making big statements.

00:00:21.836 --> 00:00:23.040
And speaking of big statements,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.500
you have to see this video
I received from a viewer.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.940
Watch this.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:27.987
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:29.820
- [Students] Hi Kelly.

00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:34.102
(students cheer)

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.510
- How about that for a welcome Ms. Kelly?

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.420
Guess what? Welcome to
Continental Elementary School

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.760
in Green Valley, Arizona.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.760
We want you to celebrate with
us today a very special event.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.920
We want to celebrate our
receiving a Guinness World Record

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.250
for

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.750
the world's

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.010
largest

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.127
handwritten thank you letter,

00:01:00.127 --> 00:01:01.500
enveloped and stamped.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.870
We are standing

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.073
on the letter right now.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.624
Look at the size of this thing.

00:01:07.624 --> 00:01:10.164
(students cheer)

00:01:10.164 --> 00:01:11.897
- I love how excited the kids are.

00:01:11.897 --> 00:01:13.080
That's so cool.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.630
The students used butcher
paper to create the letter.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.440
It's 85 feet long and
more than 50 feet wide.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.450
And it's not just about breaking records.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.090
There's a lesson behind it,
so here to tell us about it

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.890
is the man who started this project.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.320
Please welcome author
and literacy advocate,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.754
Carew Papritz, y'all, give it up.

00:01:30.754 --> 00:01:32.757
(audience cheers)

00:01:32.757 --> 00:01:33.590
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:34.423
- Nice to see me.

00:01:34.423 --> 00:01:36.106
Idina meet Asi.

00:01:36.106 --> 00:01:37.020
- Good to see you.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.880
- So this is the craziest part.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.270
So you guys actually mailed that letter?

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.318
- Yeah.

00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:44.151
- How?

00:01:44.151 --> 00:01:44.984
(audience laughs)

00:01:44.984 --> 00:01:47.430
- It was a feat, I gotta
tell you when you fold

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.690
up a letter of that size.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:49.523
- Yeah.

00:01:49.523 --> 00:01:53.070
- It's like a giant 20-foot-long burrito.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.720
It took it took 15 kids to

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.650
- [Kelly] Which also sounds good.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:56.534
- [Carew] Yeah.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.367
(Idina laughs)

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.370
- I mean look at them folding
that and, and the working

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.203
with the paper.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.850
But we said to stuff it in
the back of the postal truck

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.560
and we sent it to our sister school.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.470
The postmaster

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.320
stamped it.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.163
So it's official.

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:08.996
- [Kelly] It's official.

00:02:08.996 --> 00:02:11.040
- It official. It's an official letter.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:11.873
- I love that.

00:02:11.873 --> 00:02:13.500
They were so excited
just to hear the kids.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.474
All of them get excited to be
a part of something like that.

00:02:15.474 --> 00:02:16.307
- Oh yeah.

00:02:16.307 --> 00:02:17.140
- So how did you become an advocate

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.210
for people writing letters?

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.430
- Well this is sort of an
interesting spiritual story

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.650
but I actually worked in
the feature film industry.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.483
I actually worked

00:02:23.483 --> 00:02:25.110
on the Universal a lot
a gazillion years ago.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.130
- Oh, welcome back.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.147
- Thank you. It feels good to be back.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:31.739
But I, I became disillusioned
with the film industry.

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:32.572
- Yeah.

00:02:32.572 --> 00:02:34.080
- And I decided I just wanted
to head on out and I ended

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.820
up finding a job working as a cowboy.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.653
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:36.653 --> 00:02:38.310
- On a small, desolate
ranch, Southern Arizona.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.110
And it was like coming back to my roots.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.760
My granddad had a ranch when I grew up.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.600
- Yeah.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.000
- And, but what was
fascinating was I started

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.180
writing letters out there and
I started creating a story.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.290
And a story became a book.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.760
And the book, you know, came out.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.050
But I discovered the power of
what it was to write a letter.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.080
And what's amazing is
when you write a letter

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.490
and you put your time into it.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.478
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:00.478 --> 00:03:03.030
- You actually give, it goes
into the page, you give that

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.790
to somebody and they
give you the gift of time

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.647
- Yeah

00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:07.480
- and you receive it.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.400
So it's really an interesting thing and so

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.080
- [Kelly] You're a romantic cowboy.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.437
I like it.

00:03:11.437 --> 00:03:12.360
- Really? I am. It's really sad.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.200
- No it's not sad!

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.720
Super hot. What? No, that's great.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.340
It's, I love writing letters.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.440
I'm actually really into
like personally writing them.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.310
I do it all the time.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.480
Do y'all like writing letters?

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.670
Most people just stick to
your phone, I guess nowadays.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.503
Do y'all ever write?

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:25.560
- No, when my son goes to camp

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.150
and they make the kids write letters too

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.118
which is so important.

00:03:28.118 --> 00:03:29.680
- [Kelly] Oh I love that.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.710
- It's, yeah, it is the gift of time.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.009
It's, they're taking
time outta their day to

00:03:33.009 --> 00:03:35.790
make you important and
like send you something.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.110
That's so nice.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.180
So how did you get
involved with the school?

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.530
- Well, my son went to school there.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.363
- Yeah.

00:03:41.363 --> 00:03:42.196
- So that was really
cool and a big shout out

00:03:42.196 --> 00:03:44.610
to the school 'cause we could not do any

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.840
of this this letter

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.550
and stuff to the students, to the teachers

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.260
to the superintendent and all that.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.340
So, but what was really
cool is they allow me to

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.870
do these things and it
brings hope and positivity

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.874
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:03:58.874 --> 00:04:00.450
to the kids in a world where
it's just, they've got so

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.283
much turmoil.

00:04:01.283 --> 00:04:03.600
They've got through covid
and all this, and we do this

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.500
through letters.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.910
And so the first thing we teach them

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.791
about writing a letter is
you do it from the heart

00:04:08.791 --> 00:04:11.490
- [Kelly] And you're getting
them away from all the tech.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.600
They're born in a tech world.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.490
Right. So it's like a
real handwritten letter

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.390
- And it slows them down.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.560
Yeah. And it's not a text.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.030
It's not, and we're teaching them patience

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.350
and we're teaching them gratitude.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.395
- Yeah.

00:04:20.395 --> 00:04:21.228
- Because when you write a letter

00:04:21.228 --> 00:04:22.650
you end up giving that to somebody.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:23.483
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:23.483 --> 00:04:25.260
- And you give it to your
community or however it works.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.660
So it's, it's, it's such a cool thing

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.024
and it's not work

00:04:29.024 --> 00:04:29.940
for them.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.773
It's fun.

00:04:30.773 --> 00:04:31.650
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.600
It's the best way to immerse
them into learning something.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.433
Yeah.

00:04:34.433 --> 00:04:35.820
And to get them, inspire
them to do something.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.400
'cause like, they're not of a
generation where people wrote

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.290
you know, they, they don't
write letters generally.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:41.176
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:41.176 --> 00:04:43.043
- So I think that's really
cool to bring that back.

